export anchor HiFiReceiverStyle:
    number: 329
    screen: MusicPlayer
    name: Hi-fi receiver
    idea: The player is a stack of hi-fi components in brushed dark aluminium, with a blue backlit LCD for the song and lyrics, a machined volume knob ringed by a lit arc, small LED push buttons and a tuner dial whose presets are the queue.
    base: dark
    palette:
        rack: #0e0f11, the page, the gaps between components and the style sheet
        plate: #2a2c30, brushed faceplates, striped finely with #26282b and #2d2f33
        plateEdge: #45484e, bevels, button rims and the secondary button border
        engraving: #d6d9de, labels and button words on the plate
        etched: #a9aeb6, secondary labels and units on the plate
        lcd: #071a33, the display, the dial window and text fields
        backlight: #a6dcff, LCD text, lit LCD segments, the volume arc and the dial scale
        backlightDim: #6e9fc9, the next lyric line and unlit segment outlines
        ledAmber: #ffb84a, lit indicator LEDs, preset numbers and markers, and focus
        ledOff: #3b3e43, unlit indicator LEDs
        needle: #ff7a5c, the tuner needle marking the song now playing
    type:
        Two stacks. Engraved labels use Helvetica Neue and Arial, 12px at
        700 in caps with 0.2em tracking, with etched units at 11px and
        0.16em. The LCD uses ui-monospace, Menlo and Consolas, with the
        title at clamp 24 to 36px at 700 in caps, lines at 15px and a soft
        blue glow. Preset titles are 14px at 700.
    layout:
        A rack of three components with 8px gaps. The receiver has a 150px
        left column with Brightwork Sound, Stereo receiver and an amber
        Power on LED, a wide inset LCD in the middle, and a 200px volume
        knob on the right. The LCD reads NOW PLAYING and INPUT LIBRARY in
        small caps, then HARBOUR LIGHTS, the artist and album, a row of 32
        outlined segments with 15 filled, the elapsed and total time, and
        under a dashed rule the current lyric behind a play arrow with the
        next line dimmer. The knob is a machined dark disc with fine
        ridges and an amber dot, ringed by a blue arc lit to 70 percent,
        labelled Volume 70. Under a groove runs a row of small square keys,
        each with an icon cap and a word with an LED, Shuffle Off and
        Repeat Off on the left, Prev, a wider Pause with a lit LED and
        Next in the centre, and Liked On with a lit LED on the right. The
        tuner component shows Presets, Up next with 5 songs beside an
        LCD dial window with a fine blue scale, five amber preset marks
        numbered 1 to 5 and a coral needle before the first, then five
        raised preset buttons with an amber number, title, artist and
        time. The input component lists the playlists with song counts and
        Albums, Artists and Podcasts as raised selector buttons. Below
        980px the knob sits beside the LCD and presets wrap, and below
        620px everything stacks, the keys form a three column grid and the
        dial scrolls sideways inside its window.
    spacing: An 8px unit. 20 to 24px faceplate padding, 8px between components and 10px between keys.
    density: Medium. Each component holds one function, with tiny dense labels like real gear.
    corners: 4px plates, 2px keys and LCD windows, a round knob.
    borders: A light 1px top bevel and dark 1px bottom bevel on every plate and key, and a 2px dark ring around each LCD window.
    shadows: An inset shadow in each LCD window, a hard 0 2px 0 black step under keys and a soft blue glow on LCD text.
    icons:
        Small solid transport glyphs on key caps above engraved words.
        State is a round LED plus the word On or Off, lit amber when on.
        The current lyric has a play arrow.
    focus: A 2px amber outline offset 2px, matching the LEDs.
    tone: Engraved equipment words, such as Power on, Volume, Presets, Input and Shuffle Off.
